    47	## Recon note (parent-only)
    48	
    49	The operator's brief asked for capture, contract, preflight and one independent review. The parent read the whole seam, so no separate research child was dispatched. Budget: this preparation session; attempts consumed: 0.
    50	
    51	- **Baseline:** `origin/development` at `6142128d9c433d6b12972c6cd9a6f864f0ed9da2` (2026-11-27).
    52	- **Observed (reproduced):** in a scratch repo with `seeded/f.txt` and `seeded/sub/g.txt` committed and `seeded/f.txt` then edited, `RTL_ALLOW=("seeded")` and `rtl_worktree_begin` produce `<wt>/seeded/seeded/`, and `<wt>/seeded/f.txt` keeps the HEAD content (`v1`) instead of the host's edit (`v2`).
    53	- **Call path:** every turn shim (Python by default, e.g. `relay-automation/codex-turn.sh` → `utils/py/codex-turn.py`) reaches `rtl.py` `worktree_begin` (`utils/py/rtl.py:1156-1161`), which runs the Bash `rtl_worktree_begin` (`relay-automation/relay-turn-lib.sh:722`). Its seeding loop (`:774-791`) does `mkdir -p "$wt/$(dirname "$a")"; cp -R "$RTL_ROOT/$a" "$wt/$a"` (`:783-784`). After `git worktree add` the directory already exists, so BSD/GNU `cp -R src dst` copies **into** it. There is no separate Python seeding (the issue's "Python twin" check: `rtl.py` delegates).
    54	- **State writer / consumer:** the seed is the writer; `rtl_worktree_end` copies changed allowlisted paths back and commits them, which is how the nest reached a real lane's commits (issue, GH-1315 lane).
    55	- **Smallest plan:** directory entries only (not symlinks). Before creating or removing anything, resolve the worktree and the deepest **existing** ancestor of the entry's parent physically and require that ancestor inside the worktree (a tracked symlink in the checkout can point outside); only then `mkdir -p` the parent, resolve it again and require containment; remove an existing destination and confirm it is gone; then `cp -R`. Every failure fails the begin with no worktree path echoed, through one helper that tears down with `git worktree remove --force` only (`WORKTREE-SAFETY.md`) and, if Git refuses, reports it on stderr and leaves the worktree in place rather than raw-deleting it. Failure handoff is unchanged from a failed `git worktree add`: `rtl.py` `worktree_begin` returns None (`utils/py/rtl.py:1156-1161`), and the Python Codex caller exits 5 when isolation was requested (`utils/py/codex-turn.py:83-91`). File entries keep today's `mkdir -p` + `cp -R`. One loop plus one small helper in one file, plus regenerating `relay-pkg.tar.gz`. A contents-only overlay (`cp -R "$src/." "$dst"`) is not enough: it keeps children deleted on the host.
    56	- **Dependencies / overlap:** no open PR touches `relay-turn-lib.sh` or `relay-pkg.tar.gz`. Any other change under `relay-automation/` that regenerates the package before Run A would make this packet stale under #1664, which is the gate working as intended.
    57	- **Discriminating check:** the probe (contract below) sources the library and runs the real `rtl_worktree_begin` against a scratch repo (inherited `GIT_*` dropped, global/system git config off, `TMPDIR` inside its own temp dir, worktree removed and temp dir deleted afterwards). It exits 0 only when: the packaged `relay-pkg.tar.gz` member equals the live library; for a directory entry plus a file entry, there is no nested copy, the host edit is seeded, the nested file survives, the child deleted on the host is absent and the file entry is seeded; a directory whose copy fails (one unreadable file) makes `rtl_worktree_begin` fail; and when the checkout copy of the directory cannot be cleared (`rm` shadowed to refuse it) the begin fails with no path even though the source is readable. The readable arm requires a nonempty, existing returned worktree before checking contents. Arm 4: the checkout's parent of the entry is a tracked symlink to a directory outside the worktree while the host has a real directory; the begin must fail with no path and create nothing outside. Arm 5: a failed seed whose `git worktree remove` is refused must report the refusal and leave the worktree in place (no raw deletion). Matrix (`TESTS-RESULTS/2026-11-27+GH-1658-runA-prep/matrix.txt`): base 1; simulated source fix without regenerating the package (`sim-gh1638.patch`) 1; the same with `make-pkg.sh` (`sim-gh1638-with-pkg.patch`) 0; skip-directories fake (`fake-gh1638.patch`) 1; contents-only overlay fake (`fake2-gh1638-overlay.patch`) 1; a mirror that ignores a failed removal (`fake3-gh1638-rm-unchecked.patch`, review round 2's simulated fix) 1; a mirror that creates the parent before proving containment and raw-deletes on failure (`fake4-gh1638-mkdir-first.patch`, review round 3's simulated fix) 1. `pkg-freshness-arms.txt`: on the source-only arm `bash test/relay-pkg-freshness.sh` exits 1 (drift: `relay-automation/relay-turn-lib.sh`); after `make-pkg.sh` it exits 0.
